interp.New() injects the full standard package set per test; under double-VM (VM-interpreting-the-interpreter-that-runs-a-VM) that is ~490s/test on the CI runner (~12x slower than a dev machine), so a shard's slice blows the 45min cap — and the ~12x runner slowdown cancels the 12x test-level sharding. Double-VM adds ~no coverage over -int for the interpreter's OWN tests (they re-exercise construction -int already covers via one VM). Runs fully under -int / -comp-int / -comp.
